-- ============================================================
-- Statewide Executives — fast-follow seed (Political research fix #2,
-- continued): lieutenant governor, attorney general, secretary of
-- state, treasurer. Governors were seeded separately in
-- statewide_executives_seed.sql; this fills the remaining ~200 rows
-- documented there as a deliberate fast-follow.
--
-- Source: Ballotpedia's current officeholder lists, fetched live during
-- this session (not from model memory):
--   https://ballotpedia.org/List_of_current_lieutenant_governors_in_the_United_States
--   https://ballotpedia.org/List_of_current_attorneys_general_in_the_United_States
--   https://ballotpedia.org/List_of_current_secretaries_of_state_in_the_United_States
--   https://ballotpedia.org/List_of_current_treasurers_in_the_United_States
--
-- Coverage notes (real gaps, not scraping bugs — verify against
-- Ballotpedia directly if a row is ever in question):
--   - Lieutenant governor: no such office in Maine, New Hampshire, Oregon,
--     Wyoming (46/50 have the office); Arizona's office exists but is
--     vacant as of this seed — its first election is later in 2026 (45/46
--     currently filled).
--   - Secretary of State: no such office in Alaska, Hawaii, Utah (47/50).
--   - Treasurer: New York and Texas have a Controller/Comptroller instead
--     of a Treasurer (48/50); several states use a different title for
--     the same role (e.g. Florida's CFO, Minnesota's Commissioner of
--     Management and Budget) — the "treasurer" office key still applies,
--     office title differences are cosmetic.
--   - party is left NULL for offices Ballotpedia lists as officially
--     nonpartisan/appointed rather than guessing an affiliation.
--   - term_start is left NULL where Ballotpedia only gave a year, not a
--     full date — an approximate Jan 1 date would be wrong more often
--     than it'd be right for an "authoritative source" table.
--
-- Run once in the Supabase SQL editor, after statewide_executives_seed.sql.
-- ============================================================

ON CONFLICT (state, office) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  party = EXCLUDED.party,
  term_start = EXCLUDED.term_start,
  source_url = EXCLUDED.source_url,
  updated_at = now();
